meta {
  name: health
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/health
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq ok
}

docs {
  Process liveness and version. Despite the name this checks no dependency
  and answers the same as /live; for the state of postgres and redis use
  /ready. Reading a 200 here as "everything is healthy" is how you end up
  looking in the wrong place.

  Unauthenticated on purpose: a probe that needs a token cannot tell you the
  service is up when authentication is what broke.
}
